==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|mánuðr|lang=non}}, variant of {{term|mánaðr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*mēnōþs||month}}, from a derivative of {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*mḗh₁n̥s||moon, month}}. See also {{term|máni|lang=is}}. Cognate with Faroese {{term|mánaður|lang=fo}}, Danish and Norwegian Bokmål {{term|måned|lang=da}} and Swedish and Norwegian Nynorsk {{term|månad|lang=sv}}, English {{term|month|lang=en}}, Old English {{term|monaþ|mōnaþ|lang=ang}}, German {{term|Monat|lang=de}}, Dutch {{term|maand|lang=nl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmauːnʏːðʏr/|lang=is}}

